  "bug_description": "### 🐛 Describe the bug\n\nTracking this in Umbrella Bug: https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/162178\n\nJob link:  https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/actions/runs/17470577491/job/49628024441 \n\nThis unit test seems to be successful when running on a 4-GPU runner. But it fails to run on recently added 8-GPU runner (B200). \n\nValueError: Number of microbatches (4) must be greater than or equal to the number of stages (8).\n\nTo execute this test, run the following from the base repo dir:\n    python test/distributed/pipelining/test_stage.py StageNegativeTest.test_shape_prop_mismatch\n\nFor this purpose, I added https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/160803 require_exact_world_size(), so this test should be decorated with `require_exact_world_size(4)` to workaround this. Or someone please fix it so that it works with both 4-GPU and 8-GPU setting. \n\n### Versions\n\nTOT should reproduce this. \nThe version I used was based on pytorch commit: [145a3a7bda15e3963a33eb1b54bba5d4a270b225](https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/commit/145a3a7bda15e3963a33eb1b54bba5d4a270b225)\n\ncc @H-Huang @awgu @wanchaol @fegin @fduwjj @wz337 @wconstab @d4l3k @pragupta @ezyang @msaroufim @dcci",
